At the core of this issue is what I've considered to be a long-standing
inconsistancy in Nethack's treatment of the Elbereth engraving feature.

It wards against the great majority of monsters, basically all of them
except humans, demi-humans (including minotaurs) and a select few big
baddies.  The rationale behind that is respect, or rather its lack, for
the word.

However, many monsters who respect it aren't technically able to
respect anything, that is to say they are unable to "To feel or show
deferential regard for" or "avoid violation of or interference with"
this word, considering that they have no brain.  Gelatinous cubes, as
stated elsewhere in this thread, being just one example.  Magic, of
course, is a good answer to this, but then we should stop explaining it
in terms of respect.  Although the word might be useful in terms of
examining play mechanics (especially since the usage probably came from
comments in the source), it is still confusing.

